 Act (FOIA)\nForms and Documents\nHow Do I…\nLinks\nMap/Directions\nSt. Joseph County News & Press Releases\nOnline Payments\nPrivacy Policy\nRecycling\nStaff Directory\nSite Help\nSite Map\nSocial Media Policy\nSearch\nSearch\nMenu\nCounty Treasurer\nDelinquent Tax / Homeowner Resources\nDog License Information\nForeclosure / Tax Auction / Sale Proceeds Information\nLand Division / Combination Tax Certification\nPoverty Exemption\nProperty Tax FAQ\nContact\nCounty Treasurer\nHistoric Courthouse - Second Floor 125 W. Main St. PO Box 220\nCentreville, MI, 49032\nPhone:\n(269) 467-5525\nForms and Documents\nCounty Treasurer\nCounty Treasurer\nHome Government County Treasurer\nTasked with safeguarding the county’s financial health, the Treasurer’s Office manages everything from high-level investment strategies and debt service to daily cash flow operations. Residents interact most frequently with the office for property-related matters, such as warranty deed certifications and land division processing, as well as for obtaining annual dog licenses. Additionally, the Treasurer provides vital administrative leadership through active roles on the Plat Board, Elections Commission, and the County Building Authority.\nProperty Taxes\nUnder PA 123, you have less time to pay delinquent taxes. Properties 2 years behind face foreclosure and public auction. Pay your delinquent taxes here.\nPay Delinquent Taxes\nPrincipal Residence Exemption\nCheck your bill for the P.R.E. exemption. If you live in the property as your primary home, you may qualify for tax savings.\nDownload PRE Affidavit\nMilitary Relief\nActive military personnel may qualify for lowered interest rates on delinquent property taxes under the Soldiers and Sailors Relief Act.\nApply for Relief\nDepartment Contacts\nCounty Treasurer\nName |\nTitle |\nPhone |\nKathy Humphreys\n|\nCounty Treasurer |\n(269) 467-5525\n|\nStacie Wyatt\n|\nChief Deputy Treasurer |\n(269) 467-5525\n|\nHome\nGovernment\nServices\nAddress:\n125 W. Main St. P.O. Box 189, Centreville, MI 49032\nPhone:\n(269) 467-5500\nHours\n9AM - 5PM\nCopyright © 2026\nContact Webmaster\nContact Webmaster First Name\nLast Name\nEmail\nSubject\nYour Message\nSubmit Form\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Use\n✕ Hi! I'm Joey A.I. I can help you with questions about services offered by St. Joseph County. Just type in your question at the bottom of this screen!",
